"}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தமக்கொன்","parts":[{"text":"தமக்கொன்","lemma":"தமக்கொன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"றின்னா","parts":[{"text":"றின்னா","lemma":"றின்னா","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இரவின்","parts":[{"text":"இரவின்","lemma":"இரவின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இன்றுணை","parts":[{"text":"இன்றுணை","lemma":"இன்றுணை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யாகிய","parts":[{"text":"யாகிய","lemma":"யாகிய","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"படப்பை","parts":[{"text":"படப்பை","lemma":"படப்பை","gloss":"garden"}],"gloss":"garden"},{"surface":"வேங்கைக்கு","parts":[{"text":"வேங்கை","lemma":"வேங்கை","gloss":"Vēṅkai tree"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"கு","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to the Vēṅkai tree"},{"surface":"மறந்தனர்","parts":[{"text":"மறந்தனர்","lemma":"மற","gloss":"forgot (he)"}],"gloss":"did he forget"},{"surface":"கொல்லோ","parts":[{"text":"கொல்லோ","lemma":"கொல்","gloss":"particle of doubt"}],"gloss":"indeed?"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மறப்புரும்","parts":[{"text":"மறப்புரும்","lemma":"மறப்புரும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பணைத்தோள்","parts":[{"text":"பணைத்தோள்","lemma":"பணைத்தோள்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மரீஇத்","parts":[{"text":"மரீஇத்","lemma":"மரீஇத்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"துறத்தல்","parts":[{"text":"துறத்தல்","lemma":"துற","gloss":"abandoning"}],"gloss":"abandoning"},{"surface":"வல்லியோர்","parts":[{"text":"வல்லியோர்","lemma":"வல்லோர்","gloss":"he who is capable of"}],"gloss":"he who is capable of"},{"surface":"புள்","parts":[{"text":"புள்","lemma":"புள்","gloss":"bird"}],"gloss":"bird"},{"surface":"வாய்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"வாய்","gloss":"mouth"}],"gloss":"mouth"},{"surface":"தூதே","parts":[{"text":"தூது","lemma":"தூது","gloss":"messenger"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphatic particle"}],"gloss":"messenger?"}]}],"literal":"To us one thing he does not say, even though, to himself one thing / painful night's sweet companion who became / garden Vēṅkai tree, did he forget? / Forgetting difficult bamboo-like shoulders having embraced / abandoning he who is capable of, [is he waiting for] the bird's mouth's messenger?","translation":"Even though he does not say a single word to us, did he forget the Vēṅkai tree in our garden which became his sweet companion during those painful nights? He who is capable of embracing my bamboo-like shoulders, so hard to forget, and then abandoning me, is he now waiting for the bird's voice as a messenger?","modern":"அவர் நமக்கு ஒரு வார்த்தையும் சொல்லவில்லை என்றாலும், துன்பம் தரும் இரவுகளில் தனக்கு இனிய துணையாக இருந்த நம் வீட்டுத் தோட்டத்து வேங்கை மரத்தை மறந்துவிட்டாரோ? மறப்பதற்கு அரிய என் மூங்கில் போன்ற தோள்களைத் தழுவிவிட்டு, பின் என்னைப் பிரிந்து செல்லத் துணிந்த அவர், பறவையின் குரலாகிய தூதை எதிர்பார்த்துக் கொண்டிருக்கிறாரோ?","explanation":"The heroine speaks to her friend in the pālai (wasteland) landscape, expressing her deep sorrow over the hero's departure. She wonders if the hero, who left without saying a word, has forgotten the Vēṅkai tree in their garden. This tree had been his sweet companion during the painful nights when he secretly waited to meet her. She questions how he could so easily abandon her after embracing her beautiful, bamboo-like shoulders, which should be impossible to forget. The mention of the 'bird's voice as a messenger' suggests he might be waiting for a favorable omen to return, highlighting the irony of his silence.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}